  "description": "ROMJEK crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C64 H94 Co2 Gd4 N6 O24 2+,2(N1 O3 1-),2(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Co1 (Co) has 4 O neighbors; Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Co1A (Co) has 4 O neighbors; Gd1A (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2A (Gd) has 9 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.165-3.976 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 87.84-112.31°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C64H94N8O30Co2Gd4. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
